  461: .. function:: void arb_get_interval_fmpz_2exp(fmpz_t a, fmpz_t b, fmpz_t exp, const arb_t x)
  462: 
  463:     Computes the exact interval represented by *x*, in the form of an integer
  464:     interval multiplied by a power of two, i.e. `x = [a, b] \times 2^{\text{exp}}`.
  465:     The result is normalized by removing common trailing zeros
  466:     from *a* and *b*.
  468:     This method aborts if *x* is infinite or NaN, or if the difference between
  469:     the exponents of the midpoint and the radius is so large that allocating
  470:     memory for the result fails.
  472:     Warning: this method will allocate a huge amount of memory to store
  473:     the result if the exponent difference is huge. Memory allocation could
  474:     succeed even if the required space is far larger than the physical
