== refs/src/flint-3.0.1/fmpq.rst
   19: A fraction is said to be in canonical form if the numerator and
   20: denominator have no common factor and the denominator is positive.
   21: Except where otherwise noted, all functions in the :type:`fmpq` module
   22: assume that inputs are in canonical form, and produce outputs in
   23: canonical form. The user can manipulate the numerator and denominator
   24: of an :type:`fmpq_t` as arbitrary integers, but then becomes
   25: responsible for canonicalising the number (for example by calling
   26: ``fmpq_canonicalise``) before passing it to any library function.
  196: .. function:: void fmpq_set_si(fmpq_t res, slong p, ulong q)
  197: 
  198:     Sets ``res`` to the canonical form of the fraction ``p / q``.
  400: .. function:: void fmpq_add(fmpq_t res, const fmpq_t op1, const fmpq_t op2)
  408:     Division by zero results in an error.
  409:     Aliasing between any combination of the variables is allowed.
  410: 
  419:     Aliasing between any combination of the variables is allowed,
  420:     whilst no numerator is aliased with a denominator.
  475: .. function:: void fmpq_inv(fmpq_t dest, const fmpq_t src)
  476: 
  477:     Sets ``dest`` to ``1 / src``. The result is placed in canonical
  478:     form, assuming that ``src`` is already in canonical form.
  519: .. function:: void fmpq_gcd(fmpq_t res, const fmpq_t op1, const fmpq_t op2)
